{"season":2026,"week":9,"kind":"preview","league":"67FFL","my_team":"ATX Bowers","generated_utc":"2026-11-05T22:48Z","writer":"claude","headline":"Week 9 preview: ATX Bowers need RB help and a defense","dek":"Our projection has ATX Bowers at 110.8 points, 11th of 12 teams, so the cheap upgrades matter.","sections":[{"id":"my_lineup","title":"Your best lineup","md":"Our projection has the best lineup at **110.8** points. That ranks 11th in the league, ahead of only I Love it Ra (106.8). You're 1-7, so this is about squeezing out every point.\n\n- **QB:** Drake Maye (19.24)\n- **RB:** Aaron Jones (12.41), Jonah Coleman (11.30)\n- **WR:** Rashee Rice (12.71), Deebo Samuel Sr. (11.16)\n- **TE:** Brenton Strange (9.85)\n- **FLEX:** Denzel Boston (10.69), Jordan Addison (9.81)\n- **K:** Cairo Santos (8.17)\n- **DEF:** TB D/ST (5.45)\n\nTony Pollard is on bye, so he's out. That leaves you thin at RB, which is the weak spot. Your RB group projects at 23.7 against a league median of 30.2, and TE is 9.8 against 11.6. QB (19.2 vs 18.8) and WR (44.4 vs 42.2) are above median.\n\nMaye (shoulder), Jones (knee), Rice (hamstring) and Strange (eye) all carry injury tags, but each is listed as a full practice participant. Nothing there changes the lineup."},{"id":"close_calls","title":"Close calls","md":"**FLEX: Jordan Addison over Dalton Kincaid, by 0.03.** That's a tie.\n\n- **Addison (MIN, vs BUF):** projects 9.81. He plays 92% of snaps over the last three games, has a 20% target share and a 10.4 xFP. MIN's implied total is 21.0.\n- **Kincaid (BUF, vs MIN):** projects 9.78. His season average is 11.3, last three 11.0, and xFP over the last three is 11.1. BUF's implied total is 24.5. He's listed questionable with a chest injury.\n\nOur projection can't separate them, so health decides it. If Kincaid is active, his recent scoring and usage are better than Addison's. That's my read of the underlying numbers, not what the projection says. If he's ruled out or looks shaky, Addison is the easy call. Check his status before kickoff."},{"id":"waivers","title":"Waiver adds and streamers","md":"Your needs are RB and a defense. Most of the pool doesn't beat your starters, but two adds do.\n\n- **RB Emanuel Wilson (SEA):** projects **12.63**, above Jones (12.41) and Coleman (11.30). He's at 46% of snaps over the last three games with a 12.0 xFP, and SEA's implied total is 27.0 against ARI. He's the best pickup for you.\n- **DEF NYG D/ST:** projects **8.61** against PHI, whose implied total is just 18.0. That's about **+3.2** over TB D/ST (5.45), the biggest gain available anywhere. NO D/ST (8.24, vs CLE) is the backup option.\n- **K Daniel Carlson (NO):** 8.44 vs Santos at 8.17. A marginal upgrade, only worth it if you have a spare roster spot.\n\nNot worth the move for you:\n- **TE:** AJ Barner (9.74) and Chig Okonkwo (9.53) don't beat Strange at 9.85. Okonkwo does have a 20% target share and rising snaps (68% on the season, 75% over the last three), so he's a stash if TE matters later.\n- **WR DeMario Douglas (NE):** projects 9.70, below Addison. His last-three average (13.8) runs well ahead of his xFP (7.8), so I'd be cautious.\n- **QB:** Maye starts at 19.24 and Matthew Stafford is on your bench, so you don't need a streamer."},{"id":"buy_sell","title":"Buy low, sell high","md":"Gaps compare PPR points per game with expected fantasy points (xFP) per game. A negative gap means the player has been scoring below his usage. A positive gap means he's been scoring above it.\n\n**Hold or buy low**\n- **Jonah Coleman:** 11.0 PPR per game against 13.0 xFP (**-2.0**). He's already in your lineup and the usage is better than the results, so don't sell him.\n- **Matthew Stafford:** 16.5 against 18.3 (**-1.8**). He's on your bench behind Maye. No team in the league lists QB as a need, so the trade market for him is thin. Keeping him as insurance is fine.\n\n**Sell high**\n- **Rashee Rice:** 14.1 PPR per game against 10.3 xFP (**+3.7**). He projects 12.71 this week, so he's still useful, but he's been scoring well above his usage. He's your best trade chip.\n- **Mike Gesicki:** 12.8 against 8.6 (**+4.2**), the largest gap on your roster. He isn't in your best lineup, so selling costs you little."},{"id":"around_league","title":"Around the league: needs and trade fits","md":"The model found no direct trade fits with your roster this week. These are ideas worth a look, and the trade deadline is Week 11, so you have two weeks after this one.\n\n**Your side:** you need RB and TE. The only surplus is Stafford, and Kincaid. I wouldn't sell Kincaid, because your TE room is below median and he's a flex option.\n\n**Ideas**\n- **Game of Throws (5-3):** deepest at RB (69.3 strength) with Woody Marks (13.56) and Rachaad White (10.62) as surplus. They need WR (26.0), with Emeka Egbuka out (foot) and A.J. Brown questionable (ankle). Rice is a sell-high WR, and a Rice-for-Marks swap would be worth exploring.\n- **Moore Than A Bite (5-3):** RB strength of 62.9 and a WR need. Tyler Allgeier (8.79) is their listed RB surplus. DJ Moore is questionable with a shoulder injury and Brian Robinson is out (hamstring), so they may be less flexible than they look.\n- **Competition for RBs:** The Dakstreet Boys (1-7), Lover Boys (3-5) and I Love it Ra (5-3) also list RB as a need, so you're bidding against them for the same help.\n- **Injury watch:** DeVonta Smith (I Love it Ra) is out with a hamstring, and Kyle Monangai (Justiniscleann) is out with a thumb injury. Davante Adams (SMA) and RJ Harvey (Just Win Baby) are on IR. Those teams may be more open to a deal."}],"links":{"Drake Maye":"p:00-0039851","Aaron Jones":"p:00-0033293","Jonah Coleman":"p:00-0041496","Rashee Rice":"p:00-0039067","Deebo Samuel Sr.":"p:00-0035719","Brenton Strange":"p:00-0038935","Cairo Santos":"p:00-0031203","TB D/ST":"d:TB","Denzel Boston":"p:00-0041037","Jordan Addison":"p:00-0038994","Tony Pollard":"p:00-0035261","Dalton Kincaid":"p:00-0038933","Sam Darnold":"p:00-00348